    <item>
      <title>SF got $7M to expand its innovation team. Lurie just fired most of it</title>
      <link>https://sfstandard.com/2026/11/07/lurie-fires-innovation-office-staff-bloomberg-grant/</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://sfstandard.com/2026/11/07/lurie-fires-innovation-office-staff-bloomberg-grant/</guid>
      <pubDate>Sat, 07 Nov 2026 09:00:00 -0800</pubDate>
      <category>San Francisco</category>
      <description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://assets.sfstandard.com/image/994911177489/image_rrs77rcrip4e7bl2t3mi279f7l/-S1200x630-FPNG" alt="SF Standard image for the innovation office story" style="max-width:100%"/></p>
<p><b>Six of 10 staffers were fired Friday with no severance. City Hall won't say whether it met the conditions on Bloomberg's largest-ever city innovation grant, including a $2.38M payment due Nov. 1.</b></p>
<blockquote>&ldquo;No positions have been eliminated.&rdquo; - <a href="https://sfstandard.com/2026/11/07/lurie-fires-innovation-office-staff-bloomberg-grant/">Mayor's office statement, which did not dispute that six of 10 staffers lost their jobs</a></blockquote>
<blockquote>&ldquo;With that technology becoming more capable than it was even a couple of years ago, the Mayor's Office of Innovation should be capable of tackling a wide range of challenges.&rdquo; - <a href="https://sfstandard.com/2026/11/07/lurie-fires-innovation-office-staff-bloomberg-grant/">Charles Lutvak, Lurie spokesperson</a></blockquote>
<p>Sources: <a href="https://sfstandard.com/2026/11/07/lurie-fires-innovation-office-staff-bloomberg-grant/">SF Standard</a></p>
<p>Feedback: <a href="sms:+16506139572?&amp;body=Digest%2011/7%3A%20loved%20%22SF%20got%20%247M%20to%20expand%20its%20innovation%20tea...%22">Loved it</a> &middot; <a href="sms:+16506139572?&amp;body=Digest%2011/7%3A%20meh%20on%20%22SF%20got%20%247M%20to%20expand%20its%20innovation%20tea...%22">Meh</a> &middot; <a href="sms:+16506139572?&amp;body=Digest%2011/7%3A%20less%20like%20%22SF%20got%20%247M%20to%20expand%20its%20innovation%20tea...%22">Less of this</a></p>]]></description>
      <media:content url="https://assets.sfstandard.com/image/994911177489/image_rrs77rcrip4e7bl2t3mi279f7l/-S1200x630-FPNG" medium="image"/>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Lurie gains power - and loses excuses</title>
      <link>https://missionlocal.org/2026/11/daniel-lurie-election-city-hall-power/</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://missionlocal.org/2026/11/daniel-lurie-election-city-hall-power/</guid>
      <pubDate>Sat, 07 Nov 2026 08:00:00 -0800</pubDate>
      <category>San Francisco</category>
      <description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://missionlocal.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/9R0A3649-2-scaled.jpeg" alt="Daniel Lurie at his election watch party, photo by Genesia Ting for Mission Local" style="max-width:100%"/></p>
<p><b>Props D, E and F passed with roughly $14M in billionaire backing, handing the mayor more control over ballots, contracts and department heads. Analysts say the blame game ends here.</b></p>
<blockquote>&ldquo;These charter reform measures will make it very hard now for mayors to argue credibly that they don't have the authority to do what voters ask of them.&rdquo; - <a href="https://missionlocal.org/2026/11/daniel-lurie-election-city-hall-power/">Jason McDaniel, SFSU political science professor</a></blockquote>
<blockquote>&ldquo;He has all the power he asked for. Let's see what he does with it.&rdquo; - <a href="https://missionlocal.org/2026/11/daniel-lurie-election-city-hall-power/">Eric Jaye, Democratic political consultant</a></blockquote>
<blockquote>&ldquo;These victories are not a finish line, they are a starting point.&rdquo; - <a href="https://missionlocal.org/2026/11/daniel-lurie-election-city-hall-power/">Daniel Lurie, in his victory speech Tuesday night</a></blockquote>
<p>Sources: <a href="https://missionlocal.org/2026/11/daniel-lurie-election-city-hall-power/">Mission Local</a></p>
<p>Feedback: <a href="sms:+16506139572?&amp;body=Digest%2011/7%3A%20loved%20%22Lurie%20gains%20power%20-%20and%20loses%20excuses%22">Loved it</a> &middot; <a href="sms:+16506139572?&amp;body=Digest%2011/7%3A%20meh%20on%20%22Lurie%20gains%20power%20-%20and%20loses%20excuses%22">Meh</a> &middot; <a href="sms:+16506139572?&amp;body=Digest%2011/7%3A%20less%20like%20%22Lurie%20gains%20power%20-%20and%20loses%20excuses%22">Less of this</a></p>]]></description>
      <media:content url="https://missionlocal.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/9R0A3649-2-scaled.jpeg" medium="image"/>
    </item>
