      <description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/c3d3692d31216c33cdb6a5bf1402e4dc4b04cdc3/376_0_4319_3456/master/4319.jpg?width=1200&amp;height=630&amp;quality=85&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;precrop=40:21,offset-x50,offset-y0&amp;overlay-align=bottom%2Cleft&amp;overlay-width=100p&amp;overlay-base64=L2ltZy9zdGF0aWMvb3ZlcmxheXMvdGctZGVmYXVsdC5wbmc&amp;enable=upscale&amp;s=1857f547ba082ab55c00f36db8f33d6f" alt="Bay Area transit photo via The Guardian" style="max-width:100%"/></p>
<p><b>The Regional Transit Measure, a sales tax worth roughly $1B a year for BART, Muni, Caltrain and AC Transit, won 62% region-wide and 79% in SF. Prop H's Muni parcel tax took 74%.</b></p>
<blockquote>&ldquo;This is existential, especially for BART.&rdquo; - <a href="https://sfstandard.com/2026/11/03/bay-area-transit-tax-bart-caltrain/">Tom Radulovich, former BART board member, before the vote</a></blockquote>
